WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.176 --> 00:00:17.096
weeks later, the twins were sitting in the tree house.

2
00:00:18.277 --> 00:00:20.137
"How many eyes does a bee have?"

3
00:00:20.597 --> 00:00:21.318
asked Katie.

4
00:00:22.458 --> 00:00:24.618
Katie was reading a book about bees.

5
00:00:25.259 --> 00:00:26.899
Joy was brushing Jellybean.

6
00:00:26.919 --> 00:00:29.800
"Two," replied Joy.

7
00:00:31.128 --> 00:00:32.989
"Five," said Katie.

8
00:00:34.631 --> 00:00:35.671
She turned the page.

9
00:00:35.691 --> 00:00:37.453
"Okay," she said.

10
00:00:37.473 --> 00:00:41.776
"How many times does a bee flap its wings in a minute?"

11
00:00:42.836 --> 00:00:43.577
"A thousand?"

12
00:00:44.077 --> 00:00:44.818
guessed Joy.

13
00:00:44.838 --> 00:00:48.861
"Twelve thousand," Katie told her.

14
00:00:50.322 --> 00:00:52.623
Katie lay down and thought about bees.

15
00:00:53.824 --> 00:00:55.605
She imagined that she was a bee.

16
00:00:55.625 --> 00:00:59.068
"I'm a sleepy bee," she thought.

17
00:01:00.312 --> 00:01:01.773
Soon she was dreaming.

18
00:01:02.394 --> 00:01:05.396
She was Katie the Bee, flapping her wings.

19
00:01:06.617 --> 00:01:10.079
Other bees flew beside her, and she could hear their wings.

20
00:01:10.099 --> 00:01:13.061
"Katie!" cried Joy.

21
00:01:14.502 --> 00:01:16.023
Katie's eyes flew open.

22
00:01:16.544 --> 00:01:18.986
The pages of her book were flapping in the wind.

23
00:01:20.166 --> 00:01:21.647
Joy stood by the window.

24
00:01:22.208 --> 00:01:23.489
Jellybean was gone.

25
00:01:23.509 --> 00:01:27.732
"The sky is turning green," Joy said.

26
00:01:28.864 --> 00:01:30.725
Dark clouds hung in the sky.

27
00:01:31.825 --> 00:01:34.025
Katie got up and looked at the wind sock.

28
00:01:34.546 --> 00:01:36.846
It was flying straight out in the wind.

29
00:01:36.866 --> 00:01:40.687
"A storm is coming," she said.

30
00:01:41.407 --> 00:01:42.528
She heard a rumble.

31
00:01:42.548 --> 00:01:44.808
"Thunder! Let's go."

32
00:01:45.429 --> 00:01:47.109
The girls hurried down the steps.

33
00:01:47.129 --> 00:01:49.990
"Look!" shouted Joy.

34
00:01:50.010 --> 00:01:53.011
"Grandpa is trying to get the chickens in their coop."

35
00:01:54.211 --> 00:01:55.571
The girls ran to help.

36
00:01:56.051 --> 00:01:57.772
They chased the squawking birds.

37
00:01:59.556 --> 00:02:01.518
"Shoo!" they cried.

38
00:02:02.098 --> 00:02:03.639
Dust spun through the air.

39
00:02:03.659 --> 00:02:09.463
"Shoo!" One by one the chickens ducked through the coop door.

40
00:02:09.483 --> 00:02:12.926
"Run to the house," called Grandpa.

41
00:02:12.946 --> 00:02:14.827
"I'll be right behind you!"

42
00:02:16.468 --> 00:02:18.370
Mom was waiting on the back porch.

43
00:02:18.390 --> 00:02:22.893
"The weather service put out a tornado watch," she said.

44
00:02:24.094 --> 00:02:27.016
She held the door open and the girls rushed inside.

45
00:02:28.156 --> 00:02:30.678
The radio in the kitchen played soft music.

46
00:02:30.698 --> 00:02:33.340
"A tornado watch!"

47
00:02:33.761 --> 00:02:34.521
Katie cried.

48
00:02:34.541 --> 00:02:36.643
"We have to be on the lookout!"

49
00:02:37.844 --> 00:02:41.747
She grabbed her captain cap from a hook by the door and put it on.

50
00:02:41.767 --> 00:02:44.690
"This family is ready!"

51
00:02:45.250 --> 00:02:47.252
she declared as she went to the closet.

52
00:02:48.453 --> 00:02:52.076
She took a box from a shelf and carried it to the kitchen table.

53
00:02:52.096 --> 00:02:55.258
"Flashlight. First aid kit.

54
00:02:55.719 --> 00:02:58.116
Water. Snacks.

55
00:02:58.136 --> 00:03:00.158
Mom, are the pillows and blankets ready?"

56
00:03:01.539 --> 00:03:05.581
"Right here," said Mom, pointing to a basket under the table.

57
00:03:05.601 --> 00:03:09.984
"I wish Dad would come home," Joy said worriedly.

58
00:03:11.285 --> 00:03:15.668
Just as Grandpa opened the screen door, the music on the radio stopped.

59
00:03:16.809 --> 00:03:17.970
An announcer came on.

60
00:03:17.990 --> 00:03:23.393
"The National Weather Service has put out a tornado warning for Boone County.

61
00:03:24.474 --> 00:03:27.116
Current severe thunderstorms could produce a tornado.

62
00:03:28.396 --> 00:03:33.420
Towns in the warning include Willow Creek "A tornado warning!"

63
00:03:33.981 --> 00:03:34.821
shouted Katie.

64
00:03:34.841 --> 00:03:37.343
"That means TAKE COVER!"

65
00:03:37.363 --> 00:03:41.487
"I'll open the storm cellar," Grandpa said.

66
00:03:42.668 --> 00:03:46.291
Mom picked up her basket, and Katie picked up her box.

67
00:03:47.592 --> 00:03:49.753
"I've got the radio," said Joy.

68
00:03:51.034 --> 00:03:54.937
Outside a blast of rain and cool air hit them in the face.

69
00:03:54.957 --> 00:03:56.559
"It's so dark!"

70
00:03:57.039 --> 00:03:57.680
Katie said.

71
00:03:59.348 --> 00:04:03.792
"Dad!" shouted Joy as Dad's truck sped up the driveway.

72
00:04:04.953 --> 00:04:07.775
Grandpa held open the door to the storm cellar.

73
00:04:07.795 --> 00:04:09.957
"Hurry!" he called.

74
00:04:09.977 --> 00:04:13.020
"Magoo!" yelled Katie.

75
00:04:13.040 --> 00:04:14.421
"Come on, boy!"

76
00:04:15.101 --> 00:04:17.784
She and the dog dashed down the cellar steps.

77
00:04:17.804 --> 00:04:20.086
"Where's Jellybean?"

78
00:04:20.626 --> 00:04:21.367
cried Joy.

79
00:04:22.928 --> 00:04:25.270
Mom put an arm around Joy's shoulder.

80
00:04:25.290 --> 00:04:27.412
"Sorry, sweetie.

81
00:04:27.756 --> 00:04:31.238
There's no time to look for the cat right now," she said.

82
00:04:31.258 --> 00:04:35.140
"Oh, Jellybean Joy whispered.

83
00:04:35.741 --> 00:04:38.562
Then she and Mom followed Katie down the steps.

84
00:04:39.763 --> 00:04:41.384
Grandpa was right behind them.

85
00:04:41.944 --> 00:04:45.506
Dad pulled the cellar door shut and fastened it tight.

86
00:04:46.987 --> 00:04:49.028
Magoo shook water from his fur.

87
00:04:50.229 --> 00:04:53.010
Mom grabbed blankets and pillows from her basket.

88
00:04:53.470 --> 00:04:55.852
"Take these," she said to the twins.

89
00:04:57.028 --> 00:04:59.771
They could hear the rain pounding on the cellar door.

90
00:05:01.212 --> 00:05:02.834
Katie hugged Magoo tight.

91
00:05:03.454 --> 00:05:05.356
Joy put a pillow over her head.

92
00:05:05.376 --> 00:05:09.921
Thunder exploded, louder and louder.

93
00:05:11.162 --> 00:05:13.464
Above them, the light bulb flashed.

94
00:05:14.165 --> 00:05:15.306
Everyone looked up.

95
00:05:15.866 --> 00:05:17.428
Then it went out.
